    "table": "Table 1 (2023 Weights). Relative importance of components in the Consumer Price Indexes: U.S. city average, December 2024",
    "title": "Education and communication + Other goods and services hierarchies",
    "period": "December 2024"
  },
  "unit_note": "Relative importance as percent of All items. Rounding rationale: BLS cost-weights page (sources/bls-cpi/relative-importance-cost-weights.htm) states \"just as with the officially published relative importance, due to rounding error these weights do not perfectly sum up to the total.\" Two hierarchies in this slice exhibit larger than typical rounding gaps: the Information technology, hardware and services (r18) children's sum deviates by up to 0.009 from the declared parent in CPI-W, and the Information and information processing parent (r14) deviates by 0.009 in both columns; both absorbed under tol-0.01 per the same rationale. Haircuts and other personal care services (r35) is declared standalone: identical to its one-child parent Personal care services (r34), which becomes a leaf feeding the Personal care (r29) roll-up.",
